  "issue_date": "2024-01-05",
  "report_week": "1",
  "report_period": "Week 1 (22nd Dec to 5th Jan 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Capesize \"Highland Park\" 174/2006 SWS, China (SS 03/2026, DD 06/2024, BWTS fitted) was committed to Chinese interests at low USD 15 mill. For reference, the three-years-younger \"Mineral Ningbo\" 178/2009 SWS, China (SS/DD 07/2024) was sold a month ago at region USD 20 mill basis prompt delivery in China. Star Bulk Carriers have sold their Ultramax \"Star Bovarius\" 61/2015 DACKS, China (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted) to Greek interests at low USD 25 mill, while the one-year-younger sister vessels \"Xing He Hai\" & \"Xing Hao Hai\" 61/2016 DACKS, China (SS/DD 03/2026 & SS 03/2026, DD 03/2024, BWTS fitted both) were committed to Chinese buyers at USD 52 mill enbloc. On the Supramax sector, the \"Ikan Parang\" 56/2011 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 12/2025, BWTS fitted) of Pacific Carriers was committed at high USD 11 mill. Remind you that back in September, the \"Heilan Song\" 56/2011 Tianjin, China (SS 12/2026, DD 12/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 13,1 mill. Moreover, the \"Richmond Pearl\" 53/2009 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 06/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold for USD 10,8 mill. Note that the one-year-older \"RHL Clarita\" 53/2008 Chengxi, China (SS 03/2028, DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in October at USD 9,5 mill. Tide Line have sold their Handysize \"Agali\" 28/2013 Imabari, Japan (SS 07/2028, DD 10/2026, BWTS fitted) to undisclosed buyers for low USD 13 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Agia Irini\" 28/2013 Imabari, Japan (SS 01/2026, DD 05/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in June at USD 13,8 mill.",
    "tankers": "Glencore have committed their LR1 \"Alpine Pembroke\" 74/2010 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 11/2025, BWTS fitted) & \"Alpine Pioneer\" 74/2011 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) to Turkish buyers Advantage Tankers for USD 65 mill enbloc. Note that a month ago, the older sister vessel \"Leon Apollon\" 75/2009 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 07/2024) was sold at USD 28,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "the level of low-mid usd 10,00's fio range. A number of round trips on the same route were reported in the usd 25,000/27,000 pd range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 10,000/13,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed at the level of usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 15,000/18,000 pd. Continental trips via US Gulf into Persian Gulf were reported at the level of usd 22,000/24,000 pd. Inter- Mediterranean trips via Baltic and Red Sea were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. On the period front, a Kamsarmax were reported fixed in the usd 16,250 pd for 1 year employment basis delivery China. Also, a Kamsarmax was fixed on period at the usd 15,200 pd basis delivery China for 5/7 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 8,000/10,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips via Persian Gulf into East Coast India were reported at the level of usd 20,000/22,000 pd. An Ultramax was fixed on period at the usd 17,000 pd basis delivery China for 4/6 months employment with redelivery Singapore- Japan range.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Continental trips into West Africa were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. West African trips into East Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 6,000/8,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into North Coast South America were fixed around usd 20,000/22,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
